                            type="image/webp">


                        <source srcset="{{ 'fermetation-left-bg.webp' | file_url }}" type="image/webp">
                        <img src="{{ 'fermetation-left-bg.webp' | file_url }}" alt="The hive triad background"
                            loading="lazy" fetchpriority="low" decoding="async" width="396" height="341">
                    </picture>
                </div>

                <div class="fermetation-left-badge">
                    BEE BREAD
                </div>
                <h2 class="fermetation-left__title">
                    5х
                </h2>
                <h3 class="fermetation-left__subtitle">
                    More bioavailable than raw pollen.
                </h3>
                <p class="fermetation-left__descr">
                    Fermentation breaks the sporopollenin shell — the structure human digestion cannot crack alone.
                </p>
                <div class="fermetation-bottom">
                    <h4>
                        2,500mg
                    </h4>
                    <p>
                        per stick — <br>
                        5× the standard capsule dose
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="fermetation-right">
                <h2 class="fermetation__title title">
                    <span>Fermentation </span> <br>
                    Changes the Equation
                </h2>
                <p class="fermetation__descr">
                    Raw pollen is nutrient-dense but structurally sealed. Each grain is protected by sporopollenin — one
                    of the most chemically resistant structures in nature. Human digestion meets that wall and loses.
                    Vitamins and amino acids pass through unused.
                </p>
                <p class="fermetation__descr">
                    Bees solve it through controlled fermentation. Inside the hive, pollen mixes with nectar and enzymes
                    and enters a lactic acid fermentation cycle. Shells soften. Structure opens. Nutrients unlock.
                </p>
                <p class="fermetation__descr">
                    <strong>The result — bee bread — is pollen that already did the hard work. Proteins arrive as usable
                        fragments. Vitamins reach circulation efficiently. Enzymes retain full activity.</strong>
                </p>
                <div class="fermetation-note">
                    Bioavailability rises because structure changed — not the nutrient profile.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
